{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2","id":501915,"title":"Non-Super Evil VtR2?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-03T11:15:33-07:00","id":501915,"title":"Non-Super Evil VtR2?","content":"Having run into a mismatch between my GM skills and Vampire the Masquerade (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/501820-is-vtm-too-much-for-a-mediocre-gm\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...-a-mediocre-gm</a>), I'd like to explore moving over to the MUCH lighter setting of VtR2. However, my reading of the different groups (Circle of the Crone) makes it clear to me that the game is structured where the default game setting is &quot;you're horrible, very evil Vampires,&quot; which is fine, but doesn't let me run the &quot;dark, tortured heroes struggling with their humanity&quot; thing I love from Vampire the Masquerade 1st edition. Is there a way to reconcile the two?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:18:36-07:00","id":501935,"title":"","content":"Actually, the whole Humanity thing its actually stronger in Requiem than Masquerade, with how Humanity works, Touchstones, etc. At least that's my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:23:35-07:00","id":501942,"title":"","content":"That's what I thought too, but then the different groups (Crone, Sanctum) seem more like things I'd want to use as Antagonists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:32:22-07:00","id":501947,"title":"","content":"The assumption is that most heroic, tortured vampires will be PCs. So the All Night Society itself is pretty unpleasant, but struggling against it is absolutely a valid mode of play. And &quot;struggling&quot; can range from a <i>Blade</i>-style war to an attempt to reform one or more of the covenants.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the early part of <i>Forever Knight</i>, where Nick is a tortured hero, LaCroix is a villain, and Janette is a neutral party who caters to all elements of the vampire community, is a pretty viable setup.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 05-03-2015, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T11:50:45-07:00","id":501958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=501947#post501947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say that the early part of <i>Forever Knight</i>, where Nick is a tortured hero, LaCroix is a villain, and Janette is a neutral party who caters to all elements of the vampire community, is a pretty viable setup.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damnit, I just came into the thread to use <i>Forever Knight</i> as an example.<br /> <br /> Also, honestly, if one thinks the Lancea et Sanctum is much more evil than the Camarilla, go back and take a look at what the Camarilla really gets up to.The main difference is the Lancea et Sanctum does try to justify itself on a moral level, where the Camarilla is more like &quot;We're vampires. Humans are our subjects.&quot; What the Lancea et Sanctum often does <i>because they are monsters</i> are things the Camarilla does just because they believe it is their right.<br /> <br /> The Crone is in many ways more monstrous than the Sanctified are, but still less so than the Sabbat. Both games are filled with evil power structures - which is great, because it gives you a chance to show how not evil you are by bucking against them!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2007-wade-l","name":"Wade L","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2007_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"136"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:09:58-07:00","id":501978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=501942#post501942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I thought too, but then the different groups (Crone, Sanctum) seem more like things I'd want to use as Antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think that's kind of the point.<br /> <br /> If you look at the humanity table, you'll notice that joining up with the covenants is actually a threat to your humanity. These aren't human groups. Its all temptation, because it does make your unlife easier... for a price.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:17:01-07:00","id":501987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wade L</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=501958#post501958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Damnit, I just came into the thread to use <i>Forever Knight</i> as an example.<br /> <br /> Also, honestly, if one thinks the Lancea et Sanctum is much more evil than the Camarilla, go back and take a look at what the Camarilla really gets up to.The main difference is the Lancea et Sanctum does try to justify itself on a moral level, where the Camarilla is more like &quot;We're vampires. Humans are our subjects.&quot; What the Lancea et Sanctum often does <i>because they are monsters</i> are things the Camarilla does just because they believe it is their right.<br /> <br /> The Crone is in many ways more monstrous than the Sanctified are, but still less so than the Sabbat. Both games are filled with evil power structures - which is great, because it gives you a chance to show how not evil you are by bucking against them!</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lance, the Crone, and the Ordo all admit they are monsters. They differ on what being a monster means to them.<br /> <br /> Lance: You are cursed but given a duty by God and you will uphold that duty to the best of your ability.<br /> <br /> Crone: You are a natural part of the world and acting monstrous in the order to create growth is acceptable within reason.<br /> <br /> Ordo: You are on the first step to being a better one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:23:37-07:00","id":501997,"title":"","content":"I think it's also worth understanding that each of the Covenants offers a sort of means of justifying your own existence to yourself as well, they read like great coping mechanisms for people turned into vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T12:47:36-07:00","id":502050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=501942#post501942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's what I thought too, but then the different groups (Crone, Sanctum) seem more like things I'd want to use as Antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then use them as antagonists. Just like the original Sabbat. They play a similar role to the Roads and Paths really. Now Carthians are usually villains too, but being monsters isn't written in their manifesto. And the players don't necessarily have to be in a formal covenant. One of the sample cities basically only has the three &quot;We're a monsters and this is how we deal with it,&quot; covenants as opposed to the secular political ones, but there are still a few vampires there who refuse to get involve in their cults. The odds are against them without a covenant's resources, but couldn't the same be said for Masquerade neonates against their elders? That said, acolytes who do things like feeding on humans as little as they must have been mentioned. They can be open minded like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:19:52-07:00","id":502080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shock</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=501987#post501987\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lance, the Crone, and the Ordo all admit they are monsters. They differ on what being a monster means to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's probably worth noting that the Invictus and the Carthians know this too, and just deal with it in a different manner.<br /> <br /> The Invictus force a rigid structure through tradition, rank, comportment and oaths to control the Beast and their more monstrous aspects. The Carthians appreciate that they are different, so they should try something different than the staid neo-Feudal hierarchy of yesteryear, trying to find a medium, a structure that embraces modernity and allows for the Beast.<br /> <br /> As Leetsepeak says, the covenants are all about how to spend your time in your Requiem, and they offer some of the most long lasting and 'viable' of methods, though there's many other covenants scattered throughout the books.<br /> <br /> The Circle of the Crone doesn't have to be evil, but members are meant to appreciate that, 'You're a vampire, you're not a human anymore, so you don't have to pretend to be human. This Beast is a gift, it is your new form's owners manual, your new survival instinct.' It's all natural, this isn't a curse, so embrace it and do what thou wilt. This doesn't mean giving way wholly to the Beast, as you want to appreciate yourself, but it does mean appreciating it for the gift that it is and respecting it as part of your new 'life.'<br /> <br /> The Lancea et Sanctum are martyrs and guilt mongers. 'You don't want to be cursed, as God cursed me with this undying form, so be good, lest He send I and His other devils to punish you.' I'm biased. But the LS doesn't have to be evil, either, they can use their influence to make sure the 'righteous' succeed and the sinners find their due reward. Even if you aren't out and about doing Gods will, you can be a scholar or historian, or a moral guide to other vampires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T13:50:03-07:00","id":502133,"title":"","content":"I've actually felt for awhile that the Sanctified arguably offer one of the more sensible interpretations of the Requiem, as it justifies many of the necessities of vampiric existence and finds an appropriate spiritual context for it. I think the interpretation that they are particularly monstrous is a bit of a misreading (Evidently, one should look to Belial's Brood in both first AND 2nd edition for the monstrous part of Longinian crypto-religion), they just re-interpret normal vampiric behavior in a retributive light.<br /> <br /> The Sanctified don't just explain why you should/need to do the things you need to do to survive, it offers a purpose for it all, something I think it's easy for non-religious folks (I'm not religious myself admittedly) to discount as being important, but considering the magnitude of being Embraced, it seems fitting that many people might struggle to find a reason for being, and look at the other Covenants as not really providing a super satisfactory answer as to <i>why </i>they're Damned.<br /> <br /> In fact, the Sanctified are pretty much the only ones with a philosophy that isn't entirely self-centered, every other Covenant doesn't even begin to really figure out an appropriately important place for their human counterparts within their mainstream philosophy, while for the Sanctified, it's there from the start.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T15:06:27-07:00","id":502218,"title":"","content":"I think at <i>worst</i> the &quot;default game setting&quot; is &quot;you're kind of a dick&quot;. Most vampires settle at humanity 4 or 5. Not very nice, but not &quot;Super-Evil&quot; by any stretch of the imagination.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T16:05:18-07:00","id":502273,"title":"","content":"The core setting is &quot;you're kinda screwed, but you're kinda awesome, how we gonna do this?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T16:33:11-07:00","id":502291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502273#post502273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core setting is &quot;you're kinda screwed, but you're kinda awesome, how we gonna do this?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div> &quot;How did you get to be what you are? Were you a good girl, dragged kicking and screaming from heaven? Or a bad boy, brought back from the grave \u2019cause hell didn\u2019t deserve you? Little of both, probably.<br /> <br /> Somebody cheated death to bring you back, and now you have to make up the debt. You can devote yourself to faith and good works. Play philanthropist. Play superhero. Or you can accept that you\u2019re damned and get the party started. Piss on the cross. Get some head. Little of both, probably.&quot;<br /> <br /> You mean something like this? I absolutely fell in love with these statements in the core book Introduction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-03-2015, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T17:12:41-07:00","id":502310,"title":"","content":"Requiem 2E really stepped full-throttle on the &quot;wholly evil&quot; aspect, which was a bit of a turn-off for me. A lot of the new powers, especially Covenant-related, seem to revolve around varying levels of human sacrifice (I honestly don't think I read a single Scale that didn't involve leaving a human dead or severely injured, for just a temporary effect). Really clashes with the semi-optimistic view of Vampires I have in my Chronicle. I mean, yeah, a lot of them are bastards, but a sizeable group are just doing the best they can (or at least want to be seen that way.) Yeah, my Gotham City is run by a Mafia-styled Invictus who keeps the bad people rich and the good people scared to stay in power, but there's a Carthian Movement that's trying to take them down to restore some semblance of freedom and justice. The Carthians in my Minneapolis have a council with representatives from the other supernatural groups, specifically so everyone can try and co-operate, or at least not step on each others' toes. The Invictus of St. Paul aren't really bad, they're just Invictus.<br /> <br /> Thing is, any of the Covenants can really be portrayed as good or bad, depending on your own prejudices and how you want to run the story. Are the Lancea Sanctum really a good vampire church, offering meaning and comfort in an unlife of Damnation? Or are they complete religious zealots, crusading against anything that offends their doctrine and putting all nonbelievers (breathing or not) to the sword? Are the Circle of the Crone just vampiric pagans, seeking to get closer to the truth of nature? Or are they worshipers of dark, possibly demonic spirits that demand tribute in blood? Are the Ordo Dracul learned scholars, delving into the mysteries of the vampiric condition, or are they monsters ascendant, overcoming the few weaknesses that can slow unstoppable juggernauts of blood and death? Do the Invictus represent order and stability, or control and stagnation? Do the Carthians represent freedom and democracy, or anarchy and chaos? It's all in how you choose to interpret them.<br /> <br /> Which I guess is my biggest gripe with a lot of the new mechanics. Playing the Ordo Dracul as learned scholars seeking vampiric enlightenment is a tad difficult when most of their powers stem from research that would make Dr. Mengle say &quot;Dude, that's fucked up.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T17:57:53-07:00","id":502336,"title":"","content":"The only published scales that specifically require you to wound mortals leave them Embraced or a ghoul. Another is essentially 'torture' in exchange for removing a blood bond and another requires skin grafts, but you could take those from a mortal without killing them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-03-2015, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T18:10:42-07:00","id":502351,"title":"","content":"While I <i>hate </i>to sound like some pretentious dude about it, I really think it's unproductive to look at the Covenants and try to fit them within a binary of good/evil. As organizations, they are amoral and devoted to the Kindred existence, they're organizations for the Kindred. Hence, joining them is a breaking point, not because they're immoral, they're just not organizations made for humans, and thus serve as an obvious reminder that <i>you are not human anymore</i>. They're not really terribly friendly to humans because they're made to support beings whose survival can and often does rely on the exploitation of humans. We have organizations like these too, that allow us to live the lives we do at the expense of our fellow humans as well. I think to call them objectively good or objectively evil or anything of the sort is sort of a waste of time. Evil is not the ends of these organizations or Covenants. Survival, whatever <i>that </i>means, always is.<br /> <br /> Individually, Kindred are only as good or bad, selfish or selfless as people are. Just like in real life, there's reasons for Kindred to screw people over to get ahead, and not everyone will necessarily do that. Just like in real life, it will not always be easy for those who choose to take the high road to operate in the same arena as those who don't. It's part of the drama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":159,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","user":"Leetsepeak","date":". 05-03-2015, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T20:17:17-07:00","id":502427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502336#post502336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only published scales that specifically require you to wound mortals leave them Embraced or a ghoul. Another is essentially 'torture' in exchange for removing a blood bond and another requires skin grafts, but you could take those from a mortal without killing them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, of the core book Scales, only Mass Embrace kills anyone, and in that case, they don't quite stay dead. Fealty's Reward hurts someone badly at first, but they become a fairly advantaged ghoul. And those are both under the Mystery of the Voivode, which you can easily avoid if you want to play a character who doesn't do that sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Other Scales require substances like blood, fat, or skin, but these can all be obtained without killing anyone. People don't even need to get seriously harmed. Blood, fat, and skin can all be safely obtained via safe and unremarkable medical procedures.<br /> <br /> In <i>Secrets of the Covenants</i>, one Scale does involve taking the psychic bit of a person's brain, which is a pretty horrible thing to do, but is not fatal and may be stepped back some in the final draft. Another Scale drains a subject of blood for 10 minutes, but does no lasting harm, and significantly discounts the drained person's next Integrity or Humanity purchase. Neither of these are from Mysteries practiced by the mainstream of the Ordo Dracul.<br /> <br /> It's certainly not the stuff of Nazi medical experiments.<br /> <br /> EDIT: As for other core book covenant powers, the only one I can remember using part of a human is Curse of Babel, which <i>allows</i> you to use a human tongue, but can be more easily accomplished with beef tongue from your local supermarket. Mind you, plenty of blood sorcery can be <i>used </i>to hurt people, and anything that uses Vitae ultimately requires lethal damage somewhere along the line, but this is no different from 1e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 05-04-2015, 12:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T20:40:53-07:00","id":502449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502291#post502291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;How did you get to be what you are? Were you a good girl, dragged kicking and screaming from heaven? Or a bad boy, brought back from the grave \u2019cause hell didn\u2019t deserve you? Little of both, probably.<br /> <br /> Somebody cheated death to bring you back, and now you have to make up the debt. You can devote yourself to faith and good works. Play philanthropist. Play superhero. Or you can accept that you\u2019re damned and get the party started. Piss on the cross. Get some head. Little of both, probably.&quot;<br /> <br /> You mean something like this? I absolutely fell in love with these statements in the core book Introduction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad you liked that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was actually from my original pitch for Second Edition, a long time before <i>The Strix Chronicle</i>, <i>Sexmurder</i>, or <i>Blood and Smoke</i> were ever things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T21:56:36-07:00","id":502512,"title":"","content":"I personally feel like its a feature that the Covenants are kind of unappealing to someone trying to be a &quot;good&quot; vampire. Many neonates are likely to have exactly the same reaction, and be pretty hesitant to get involved with any of them.<br /> <br /> But the fact is that vampires <i>are</i> monsters. Feeding hurts people; sometimes only a little, sometimes more than a little. So, at the very least, every vampire is a serial assaulter. Picking up a mortal in a bar under false pretenses and proceeding to injure and abandon them is arguably sexual assault. And, eventually, every vampire loses control, and somebody dies. There's a decent chance that, when this happens, the victim is someone the vampire cares about.<br /> <br /> It could be argued that the most moral thing for a vampire to do is to end their own unnatural existence as soon as possible. <i>Perhaps</i> they can manage to do more good than ill with their Requiem, at least for a while. But eventually the burden is likely to become too much to bear, and many may get to that point pretty quickly after their embrace. That's where the Covenants come in: they give the vampire a way to make sense of the harm they've done to people, and to &quot;live&quot; with it.<br /> <br /> Joining a Covenant is a way for a vampire to save themselves from total self-destruction, and all it costs is a little piece of their fraying soul...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T22:40:26-07:00","id":502529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502512#post502512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That's where the Covenants come in: they give the vampire a way to make sense of the harm they've done to people, and to &quot;live&quot; with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. They help you cope by providing a framework for your predatory existence. A reason to do stuff. A reason to stay sane beyond just feeding and surviving. Though they help with that, too.<br /> <br /> I don't think it's really about how much a neonate <i>wants </i>to join the All-Night Society. It's either join it, or be totally alone. Or worse, have the All-Night Society actively trying to kill you. Some people prefer to be alone. These are the Nomads and the Unaligned. Their existence is <i>not easy</i>. Is it any wonder most Kindred will find a coterie or a covenant or <i>something </i>to belong to? Sure, maybe there are some things they do that horrify you, but it's better than being alone. Slowly, you learn to cope with it. Or you take to it quickly. Some people never quite shake the fact that what they do is monstrous, but I'd bet the reason most Kindred aren't just immediately ashing themselves is because they learn to accept it too.<br /> <br /> Humans will do ugly things to survive. Is it any surprising the Kindred will do the same?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T01:58:23-07:00","id":502629,"title":"","content":"I think the fiction, in the clan books and novels, seemed to imply that there were a lot more unaligned in the world than one might think based on the more mechanically inclined books. Or at least that not all members of covenants are really gung-ho about it and may just use it for the advantages such social clubs offer.<br /> <br /> To me vampire is one of the better games when it comes to allowing you to play a character as malevolent or benevolent as you want. Certainly your humanity can suffer for some deeds, but a covenant can have a vampire who arranges to get sacks of blood from a nearby hospital and only feasts on cherished pets who they in turn grant the benefits of a ghoul, alongside another vampire who keeps a bunch of hobos locked in their basement for entertainment and midnight snacks and who enjoys drinking from people until they barely have life in them. In some of the other games, you're not just deterred from that but you have to join a special 'bad guy' group to manage sort of thing.<br /> <br /> Certainly vampire has Belial's Brood but you don't have to be one of them to be a monster, if you so desire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-04-2015, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T07:17:51-07:00","id":502878,"title":"","content":"Guess I need to re-read some sections of Requiem 2E. I came away with a VASTLY different impression than others, or what was apparently intended.<br /> <br /> My bad. Carry on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T07:27:19-07:00","id":502882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502449#post502449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Glad you liked that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was actually from my original pitch for Second Edition, a long time before <i>The Strix Chronicle</i>, <i>Sexmurder</i>, or <i>Blood and Smoke</i> were ever things.</div> </div> </div> </div> It sold me on the new edition when I saw it on the free rpg pamphlet. It is absolutely beautiful. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T07:27:26-07:00","id":502883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Fealty's Reward nearly kills someone, but brings them back as a ghoul that'll go vamp if killed. Its a kind of early Embrace situation.</div> </div> </div> </div>It brings them back as a <i>draugr. </i>That's... not really the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T07:30:04-07:00","id":502885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502310#post502310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem 2E really stepped full-throttle on the &quot;wholly evil&quot; aspect, which was a bit of a turn-off for me. A lot of the new powers, especially Covenant-related, seem to revolve around varying levels of human sacrifice (I honestly don't think I read a single Scale that didn't involve leaving a human dead or severely injured, for just a temporary effect). Really clashes with the semi-optimistic view of Vampires I have in my Chronicle. I mean, yeah, a lot of them are bastards, but a sizeable group are just doing the best they can (or at least want to be seen that way.) Yeah, my Gotham City is run by a Mafia-styled Invictus who keeps the bad people rich and the good people scared to stay in power, but there's a Carthian Movement that's trying to take them down to restore some semblance of freedom and justice. The Carthians in my Minneapolis have a council with representatives from the other supernatural groups, specifically so everyone can try and co-operate, or at least not step on each others' toes. The Invictus of St. Paul aren't really bad, they're just Invictus.<br /> <br /> Thing is, any of the Covenants can really be portrayed as good or bad, depending on your own prejudices and how you want to run the story. Are the Lancea Sanctum really a good vampire church, offering meaning and comfort in an unlife of Damnation? Or are they complete religious zealots, crusading against anything that offends their doctrine and putting all nonbelievers (breathing or not) to the sword? Are the Circle of the Crone just vampiric pagans, seeking to get closer to the truth of nature? Or are they worshipers of dark, possibly demonic spirits that demand tribute in blood? Are the Ordo Dracul learned scholars, delving into the mysteries of the vampiric condition, or are they monsters ascendant, overcoming the few weaknesses that can slow unstoppable juggernauts of blood and death? Do the Invictus represent order and stability, or control and stagnation? Do the Carthians represent freedom and democracy, or anarchy and chaos? It's all in how you choose to interpret them.<br /> <br /> Which I guess is my biggest gripe with a lot of the new mechanics. Playing the Ordo Dracul as learned scholars seeking vampiric enlightenment is a tad difficult when most of their powers stem from research that would make Dr. Mengle say &quot;Dude, that's fucked up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, I feel you! I hate going full evil on my chronicles and I mean this, I understand what you're trying to say and respect it.<br /> <br /> But I must asd, with the wisdom my age of 25 has conferred upon me, have you <i>ever</i> been in a room filled with movers and shakers of the business world? Have you attended a communist, anarchist or any sort of radical (as in advocating a radical new model) organisation? Nevermind, have you ever had an off-the-record talk with a high-ranked politician of a mainstream political party? Did you ever meet someone from the mafia?<br /> <br /> Damn my bad luck, I can answer yes to most. What you describe in your post, I accept wholeheartedly and feel certain that these must be some great stories you're running, constitute an improved version of the real world (forget about the World of Darkness). A lot of these things happen under the table, but I can tell you there are some nasty stuff out there. Check the Business Plot in the US, the British Westminster child abuse ring scandal. Have you been to a parliament or congress during recess? You can even see commies sit with the neocons, chatting, laughing and being sexist together, while deep down they'd love nothing more but to be at each other's throats. Had a conversation with a board member for a large, multinational communications firm (well, its headquarters in Greece anyways) and the guy was scary. &quot;We'd love nothing more but to destroy the planet if we could make a buck out of it and get away with it!&quot; scary.<br /> <br /> That said, I have myself indulged in the semi-optimistic angle before! So don't pay too much attention to what I say. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Hell, even Nines from Bloodlines (set in gloomy cWoD) was an upstanding guy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":59,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","user":"stylanski","date":". 05-04-2015, 10:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T09:15:29-07:00","id":502991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502885#post502885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hell, even Nines from Bloodlines (set in gloomy cWoD) was an upstanding guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nines and Smiling Jack are Carthian movers and shakers in my Gotham City, standing up to the Invictus Mafia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T05:21:56-07:00","id":504061,"title":"","content":"The crones are blood witches. You could do a version with pagan theban for more alturistic pagans.<br /> Ordo started as a group trying to become the a better monster/ evolved being.<br /> While I get the Nick Knight thing, where is the disney vamp thing that keeps popping up coming from?<br /> <br /> I will say this, if you tweak the sunlight chart above humanity 7 and play with cold blood rules you can do a coping game.<br /> But the pit does yawn in front of them. Blood banking at BP 2 or 3 gets problematic.<br /> Maybe someone develops a regiment or system that helps adherents stay on that path.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T05:31:51-07:00","id":504065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502427#post502427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Other Scales require substances like blood, fat, or skin, but these can all be obtained without killing anyone. People don't even need to get seriously harmed. Blood, fat, and skin can all be safely obtained via safe and unremarkable medical procedures.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, so does that mean vampire Tyler Durden has shifted from the Lancea et Sanctum to the Ordo Dracul?<br /> <br /> .... Makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T08:23:02-07:00","id":504178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=504061#post504061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I get the Nick Knight thing, where is the disney vamp thing that keeps popping up coming from?</div> </div> </div> </div>What Disney vamp thing?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T09:47:10-07:00","id":504309,"title":"","content":"Good advice all. I don't need the vampires to be nice, just more dark and tortured (at least a bit) forced to make interesting choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T10:49:14-07:00","id":504379,"title":"","content":"I don't think ANYONE'S saying &quot;Disney Vamp.&quot; We all agree that Vampires aren't all smiles and cuddles and good intentions. But we're also not looking for Buffy Vamp, &quot;You're what, shocked and disappointed? I'M EVIL!&quot; vampires, either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:35:37-07:00","id":504437,"title":"","content":"Well, we have those. They're just not PCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T11:55:05-07:00","id":504449,"title":"","content":"I've never gotten to play Vampire, I ST it, but I'd totally play an evil vampire. Though I'd probably eschew an army of hobo sex and blood slaves and lean more towards something like Belial's Brood, I guess there's some overlap if you wanted a low class Throne of Smokeless Fire or a Scarlet Rite vampire straight out of Edward Lee, complete with hock parties and headers.<br /> <br /> I always had fun running the various Brood members as NPCs, though they never succeeded in luring anyone over.<br /> <br /> And I know some people do like playing vampire sans angst or who think angst is a bad thing and instead want to play sort of more standard urban fantasy protagonists, with access to blood supplies and maintaining low Blood Potency so they can eat from animals in a hurry or deciding to feast 'only from bad guys.' I just don't think they've been mentioned here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-05-2015, 02:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T16:33:48-07:00","id":504766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But we're also not looking for Buffy Vamp, &quot;You're what, shocked and disappointed? I'M EVIL!&quot; vampires, either.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't really see anything in the Covenents that compels vampires to alternate between breaking the necks of and sucking dry every single person they come across. The closest analogue I can find is how the Master's cult was eventually developed to have an idea of &quot;we live underground because it brings us closer to the Old Ones and we forsake human society because pretending to be them is a perversion&quot;, and they might have actually been the <i>least</i> arbitrarily murderous ones in practice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-05T17:21:31-07:00","id":504828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=504065#post504065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, so does that mean vampire Tyler Durden has shifted from the Lancea et Sanctum to the Ordo Dracul?<br /> <br /> .... Makes sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tyler Durden is a Venture with Malk or a Hollow Mekhet Carthian who based his Herd of Fascism and Anarcho-primitivism.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T05:54:11-07:00","id":505303,"title":"","content":"I envy those who, upon reading Vampire, cannot see how the experience of Vampirism (even as a neonate) would not blur the lines between good and evil, sanity and madness. I've had relationships that did worse than that... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously though, there's a reason most Kindred settle around a Humanity 3-4 rating, and there are certain consequential behaviours that arise from this. I still use this video (<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) to introduce new players to the World of <b>Darkness</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OEi7nQbNDog\" data-code=\"OEi7nQbNDog\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/OEi7nQbNDog/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> When those new players start complaining that my world is not dark enough, it is too late to realise the monsters I've created. But oh well, this serves as a focus check when I dwell too deep into dark superhero (i.e. chronicles where players and some NPCs are expected to act more ethically than real-life people would, plus disciplines) territory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T19:10:25-07:00","id":506326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=504178#post504178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What Disney vamp thing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep seeing things about running vamps sans horror. Running vamps without powers of the blood. Vamps that don't have to feed as often etc etc.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T20:43:07-07:00","id":506366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=506326#post506326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Keep seeing things about running vamps sans horror. Running vamps without powers of the blood. Vamps that don't have to feed as often etc etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. I understand that, cause I don't like it myself.<br /> <br /> But, like I said I like playing evil characters. And I like running games with a lot of dark and sexual subject matter. A lot of people don't like that or think it's wrong or the game isn't made for it. So I don't think anyone's really doing it wrong, just doing it the way they want, and not necessarily the way I want. When it comes down to it, as long as everyone's straight with each other when joining a table about what they're expecting, we should just keep playing what we want.<br /> <br /> And like I said, vampire's good for that in allowing you to be as Disney or as Blumhouse or Troma or Brazzers as you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T15:30:39-07:00","id":511234,"title":"","content":"Even cold blood isn't a kindly act considering you're swapping from taking an involuntary blood donation from the wrist of healthy people (now you can hear heart rates that would vastly improve their chances of survival) to taking way way more blood that has already been given for necessary blood transfusions that could save lives. Technically, unless you boost the rates of blood donation to well above organisational needs (which could be done), you're actually causing more death by drinking cold blood because there are all of those people who won't get life saving blood transfusions because of how much you've had to drink.<br /> <br /> It actually takes quite a bit of power and influence to feed well, easily and nicely.... Which makes for good bait. You want to be a good person? You may need to do some off colour things. Just think about what you need to groom a Rack -- the illusion of safety and security, but without the sense of community to back it up. You don't want randoms getting involved if you need to kick somebody. You want a set up similar to what a mugger needs, dark places between stretches of light, and people dumb enough and drunk enough to move through those ambush points. After all, not everyone (especially Nosferatu) are set up to seduce the blood off a person.<br /> <br /> Of course, this doesn't necessarily make a person any more evil than an organisation that crushes the nicer kindergarten down the road so that they can get more clients for their low expense / high profit child care institution or anything like that. Nasty, yes, but not necessarily &quot;evil&quot; on the level of serial killers and Mengele.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My horror roleplaying blog with a strong focus on World of Darkness and Call of Cthulhu can be found here: <a href=\"http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/\" target=\"_blank\">http://stwildonroleplaying.blogspot.com.au/</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1248-laraqua","name":"Laraqua","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T03:01:54-07:00","id":511855,"title":"","content":"I was kind of under the impression that drinking from blood bags doesn't really even work as of 2e. At the most generous interpretation (you need 2*BP pints from blood bags per Vitae, as opposed to it just being useless, which i think are both valid interpretations of the way the text is worded), you need twice as much blood at BP 1 from blood bags than you would if you drank from a human. The ratio gets worse as you get more powerful and older. So yeah, you can either take a little sip from a human who might not even notice it happened, or you can chug down multiple bags for a single Vitae and potentially rob someone of life-saving medical care. In VtR 2e, I don't think blood bags are the ethical option for a vampire.<br /> <br /> Still. Always murdering animals to try, or taking small sips from (ideally) willing humans.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T04:53:26-07:00","id":511896,"title":"","content":"On using blood bags keeping them from being used for important measures. Organizations that collect blood also sell it, and still constantly collect it because it isn't viable when stored past a certain point. Getting into that isn't likely to be that harmful unless, yes, you're a high blood potency vampire who insists on downing dozens of bags a day.<br /> <br /> But ideally at that point one has made peace with the fact that there's nothing wrong with drinking from people themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T05:17:33-07:00","id":511920,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think blood bags aren't necessarily something you go looking to for ethical reasons. They're still useful in a pinch though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:06:17-07:00","id":511943,"title":"","content":"You're looking at this from strictly mechanical perspective. Ethical reasons? How is it ethical to be attacking the individual right up front? Why not drink some blood... whoever suffers for this isn't here, I don't get to meet him, etc. While yes, logic says that you're doing more harm... but it's harm done elsewhere. Harm done where I do not see it. It's happening all the time in our world. Most of us choose the easy choice of buying cheap stuff made in china, without considering that this feeds the abuse loop of Chinese workforce. <br /> Humans choose the bigger evil elsewhere, instead of a small evil in their presence all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:15:22-07:00","id":511946,"title":"","content":"You know what? I actually think this works in-character. The neonates are all &quot;lets get blood bags so we don't have to bite anyone&quot; while older vamps take the more detached view of &quot;you know, you're doing more harm in the long run. Just take it from the source&quot;. And objectively speaking, the older vamps are right, but the young ones won't really care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T06:59:13-07:00","id":511972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=511943#post511943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're looking at this from strictly mechanical perspective. Ethical reasons? How is it ethical to be attacking the individual right up front?</div> </div> </div> </div>Feeding doesn't necessitate attacking your food. There's violent and non-violent feeding in VtR for a reason. Taking blood from someone doesn't necessitate harm, either. A vampire can sip one or two Vitae worth of blood without any real adverse side-effects. Chronic feeding from the same human may have deleterious long-term side-effects, but you can have a little fling with a human and nibble and then leave it at that with no measurable physical harm done. It's like if you cut yourself with a knife while cooking. You can lose a lot of blood, but you'll probably only need stitches, not a blood transfusion. And the vampire takes care of the stitches for you.<br /> <br /> Vampires are parasites, but I'm pretty convinced you can feed ethically, particularly with a willing herd, which implies informed consent. I don't really think you can ethically steal from a blood bank, and finding a way to do it legit would be far more effort than it's worth nutritionally to a vampire.<br /> <br /> Of course, just because a vampire <i>can</i> feed ethically doesn't mean most can or will, but this little tangent started with the morality of drinking cold blood, so that's what I'm presenting my views on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T08:52:00-07:00","id":512024,"title":"","content":"Of course the morality of drinking cold blood becomes irrelevant after a few centuries when human blood will no longer sustain you.<br /> <br /> Even the covenants don't advocate drinking from other vampires","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:04:54-07:00","id":512030,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=511972#post511972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Feeding doesn't necessitate attacking your food. There's violent and non-violent feeding in VtR for a reason. Taking blood from someone doesn't necessitate harm, either. A vampire can sip one or two Vitae worth of blood without any real adverse side-effects. Chronic feeding from the same human may have deleterious long-term side-effects, but you can have a little fling with a human and nibble and then leave it at that with no measurable physical harm done. It's like if you cut yourself with a knife while cooking. You can lose a lot of blood, but you'll probably only need stitches, not a blood transfusion. And the vampire takes care of the stitches for you.<br /> <br /> Vampires are parasites, but I'm pretty convinced you can feed ethically, particularly with a willing herd, which implies informed consent. I don't really think you can ethically steal from a blood bank, and finding a way to do it legit would be far more effort than it's worth nutritionally to a vampire.<br /> <br /> Of course, just because a vampire <i>can</i> feed ethically doesn't mean most can or will, but this little tangent started with the morality of drinking cold blood, so that's what I'm presenting my views on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's the fact that each point of Vitae you take (and 1 is the bare minimum) will deal an equal amount of Lethal damage. We are not talking as a bruise but a stab level of harm here. Something that would take at least 2 days to heal, wich is twice the time it takes for a vampire to need another drink.<br /> <br /> I mean, it takes a lot of work not to seriously harm anyone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:30:11-07:00","id":512051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=511972#post511972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Feeding doesn't necessitate attacking your food. There's violent and non-violent feeding in VtR for a reason. Taking blood from someone doesn't necessitate harm, either. A vampire can sip one or two Vitae worth of blood without any real adverse side-effects. Chronic feeding from the same human may have deleterious long-term side-effects, but you can have a little fling with a human and nibble and then leave it at that with no measurable physical harm done. It's like if you cut yourself with a knife while cooking. You can lose a lot of blood, but you'll probably only need stitches, not a blood transfusion. And the vampire takes care of the stitches for you.<br /> <br /> Vampires are parasites, but I'm pretty convinced you can feed ethically, particularly with a willing herd, which implies informed consent. I don't really think you can ethically steal from a blood bank, and finding a way to do it legit would be far more effort than it's worth nutritionally to a vampire.<br /> <br /> Of course, just because a vampire <i>can</i> feed ethically doesn't mean most can or will, but this little tangent started with the morality of drinking cold blood, so that's what I'm presenting my views on.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes, and since willing herd comes so easily with no unethical things done to them. You know dominate, vincullum, or even kiss addiction are such wonderful ethical things to do. Without these you won't find that many willing participants <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And as Thorbes pointed out, even if you drink just one vitae from each victim, you're still harming them sufficiently for the harms impairment to last two days. The actual damage lasts for longer (as has been said in some book / devs). <br /> <br /> There is no ethical feeding. Just the things vampires keep telling themselves to feel better in the end of the night <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And you know, saying &quot;well, this person gave up the blood willingly. This blood bank even pays them, so really, I'm doing no harm.&quot;. Saying that to yourself is so much easier than actually confronting the harm you're doing AND then going out to do the harm to people directly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:44:21-07:00","id":512066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512051#post512051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, and since willing herd comes so easily with no unethical things done to them. You know dominate, vincullum, or even kiss addiction are such wonderful ethical things to do. Without these you won't find that many willing participants <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And as Thorbes pointed out, even if you drink just one vitae from each victim, you're still harming them sufficiently for the harms impairment to last two days. The actual damage lasts for longer (as has been said in some book / devs). <br /> <br /> There is no ethical feeding. Just the things vampires keep telling themselves to feel better in the end of the night <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And you know, saying &amp;quot;well, this person gave up the blood willingly. This blood bank even pays them, so really, I'm doing no harm.&amp;quot;. Saying that to yourself is so much easier than actually confronting the harm you're doing AND then going out to do the harm to people directly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That strikes me as more tragic than evil though, which is what the OP wanted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T09:58:32-07:00","id":512094,"title":"","content":"We as people don't seem to mind killing plants and animals to feed. Granted there's a lot of people with issues about hurting animals but it's not as if plants aren't living things chopped to pieces to make salads and eggs aren't unborn babies smashed on a skillet to make a breakfast. At least humans tend to survive the feeding process, and even feel good from it. They can even be granted limited immortality through ghouldom, which would even stop lethal illnesses from ravaging their bodies.<br /> <br /> Why hold vampires to higher standards than you would humans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-12-2015, 01:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:03:28-07:00","id":512100,"title":"","content":"While I do understand you argument here, <i><b>Nofather</b></i>, there is a fundamental difference (though not a very large one, I admit) from me having a nice steak dinner (Beef or Bison, your pick) and carving up Eddard Stark to get my next meal. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />:","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:05:04-07:00","id":512101,"title":"","content":"He died either way. I'm guessing you read my pre-edit post where I pointed out that vampires can leave their prey alive with a full life ahead of them, the same thing can't be said about a cow or bison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:12:00-07:00","id":512104,"title":"","content":"Gotta say, I don't really see how a bit of blood-letting is unethical in the grand scheme of things. Better a nip here and there than hitting empty and ripping some poor schmuck's throat out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:17:32-07:00","id":512108,"title":"","content":"Even if you don't think you're hurting someone a lot, it still involves either forgoing their consent in the form of subtle feeding, or even if they explicitly give you consent, that consent is rendered dubious or null by the addictive nature of the Kiss.<br /> <br /> So it's not just about actual injury, it's about the violation of another person. What you do to them can't really be consented to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:24:30-07:00","id":512112,"title":"","content":"And no matter how shallowly you try to feed, the bottom line is that what you are doing to another person risks their death. It doesn't take much for things to go sideways. Just because it usually doesn't happen, doesn't mean it isn't a risk every time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:25:54-07:00","id":512114,"title":"","content":"This is why you need a werewolf buddy. They're immune to the Kiss and they'll recover from a standard feeding in 30 minutes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T10:58:30-07:00","id":512141,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512112#post512112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And no matter how shallowly you try to feed, the bottom line is that what you are doing to another person risks their death. It doesn't take much for things to go sideways. Just because it usually doesn't happen, doesn't mean it isn't a risk every time.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what if you don't drink from someone and they don't feel a little light-headed and decide to get in their car and drive and someone smashes into them with an 18 wheeler and they die? Risk is just a part of life. By this logic, you'd be more 'ethical' chaining people up in your basement. That way they'd be completely safe and you could keep track of how much blood they lost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512108#post512108\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if you don't think you're hurting someone a lot, it still involves either forgoing their consent in the form of subtle feeding, or even if they explicitly give you consent, that consent is rendered dubious or null by the addictive nature of the Kiss.<br /> <br /> So it's not just about actual injury, it's about the violation of another person. What you do to them can't really be consented to.</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's horrible and all from our perspective, but why should a vampire care? Do we get the agreement of animals and plants before we kill them? Do animals knowingly sign up for slavery before they get put in a pet store window?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-12-2015, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:16:53-07:00","id":512150,"title":"","content":"Vampires may not be strictly human anymore, but they're still people. Hence that little thing we call Humanity. The notion that they are so separate and distinct from humans is a survival mechanism for emotionally distancing themselves from the thing they have to prey on by necessity. Just because you tell yourself that doesn't mean you'll believe it wole-heartedly.<br /> <br /> Vampires violate conventional morality all the time as a necessity of their existence. That doesn't mean they're so completely divorced from that conventional morality that they can't or won't recognize the implications of their actions. That's the horror of descending Humanity. You don't start uncaring, you learn how to be as a survival mechanism, it's part of the horror.<br /> <br /> Really, the key is that they're not human but they're still people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:22:07-07:00","id":512153,"title":"","content":"And people do a hell of a lot worse than vampires might when it comes to taking a few pints of blood.<br /> <br /> The point of the game is forging a place for your own. The covenants exist to help with that, as they are mostly organizations of people who have decided that they know how vampires should act.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:32:03-07:00","id":512161,"title":"","content":"There's risk getting into 2,000 lbs of steel that races along at 75 mph.<br /> <br /> Taking blood from people to prolong your (arguably) unnatural, parasitic existence doesn't exactly fit the same mold.<br /> <br /> Yes, if you feed from someone, and that damage you dealt to them ends up causing their death, you are responsible.<br /> <br /> EDIT: This is getting into a silly philosophical area. My point is that vampires are not doing their vessels any favors, no matter how you slice it. At the base they are draining life from people to sustain themselves, and that is a bad thing in the grand scheme. There's wiggle room as to <i>how</i> bad it is, or how bad it can become, but it's not comparable to mortals consuming food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","user":"Smarmy Vamp","date":". 05-12-2015, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T11:55:41-07:00","id":512174,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512161#post512161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> At the base they are draining life from people to sustain themselves, and that is a bad thing in the grand scheme. There's wiggle room as to <i>how</i> bad it is, or how bad it can become, but it's not comparable to mortals consuming food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be more comparable and ethically pure if they just had farms where humans were raised solely so they could be drained of life by vampires?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:00:15-07:00","id":512180,"title":"","content":"No. If this is going to come down to a discussion on whether a cow's life is the equivalent of a human life, I don't think we're going to get anywhere. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:03:39-07:00","id":512183,"title":"","content":"So what makes a cow's life worth less than a human?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:16:38-07:00","id":512193,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512183#post512183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what makes a cow's life worth less than a human?</div> </div> </div> </div>Objectively nothing. But we are humans, so we tend to value the lives of our own species over the lives of other species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:17:05-07:00","id":512195,"title":"","content":"Well, at the most basic level I don't equate animal life with human life because of acculturation. <br /> <br /> I view them as lesser, subservient beings. By no means do I advocate cruelty toward animals, but my definition of cruelty will differ from some other people's. <br /> <br /> You could argue the veracity of the line I draw between humans and animals, but I don't think that will be a productive discussion. I'm not open to changing my views on the subject.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:21:52-07:00","id":512203,"title":"","content":"I don't care about your personal views beyond how a cow is worth less than a human. They really don't matter for this.<br /> <br /> The problem is you're basing vampires on human sets of ethics. Which they shouldn't be held to. Vampires have their own ethics. This is something vampires deal with, it's part of the very game.<br /> <br /> @Aiden Just like vampires are likely to value the lives of their own kind over the lives of others, like with the third tradition.<br /> <br /> @Smarmy Vamp And just like vampires are likely to view humans as lesser beings. And even then, they wouldn't necessarily advocate cruelty towards them, but the Kiss feels good, and you can drink freely from a person without killing them or setting them on the path to destruction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:24:28-07:00","id":512206,"title":"","content":"Doesn't matter what the vampire thinks, as much as it does what we playing the game think. <br /> <br /> The vampire can think it's a-okay to mow down people in a parking lot because he has to get somewhere fast, but he still bears the consequences for those actions. If you want to change that base assumption of the humanity system, that's fine. But those sorts of theme changes are based on what we as people playing a game think, and not about what the fictional characters in the stories we tell think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:26:19-07:00","id":512207,"title":"","content":"Also, very few vampires originate in a culture that views vampires as superior to humans. Sure, some vampires get there, but they're represented as detached, and therefore low-humanity.<br /> <br /> The vampire is to human as human is to cow analogy doesn't hold up, except as a rationalization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:30:17-07:00","id":512210,"title":"","content":"The only rationalization you need is &quot;I require this substance to maintain my existence&quot;. And then go about obtaining it in the manner that causes the least harm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:33:33-07:00","id":512215,"title":"","content":"Absolutely, Elfive.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying that every point of Vitae you feed from a mortal requires a detachment check. I'm just saying that the act of feeding is, at its core, negative. It's perpetuating harm on living, breathing people.<br /> <br /> I think the base assumptions of the game support that, it's one of the core themes. You need to hurt people to sustain yourself. All the time. Every night in some cases. How are you going to deal with that?<br /> <br /> It doesn't necessarily make a given vampire irredeemably evil, but it does start him off in the red.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T12:52:36-07:00","id":512225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512210#post512210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only rationalization you need is &quot;I require this substance to maintain my existence&quot;. And then go about obtaining it in the manner that causes the least harm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I've pointed out couple of pages beforehand... &quot;least harm&quot; is not the way people usually go about things. More often they go about things with &quot;more convenient or bad stuff happens elsewhere&quot; course of actions. <br /> Anyways, if we want to equalize this a bit.. we can look at this this way: &quot;If a human is starving, will he attack people out in the streets to get his food?&quot; Most people would resort to whatever they think they can get away with in the situation and whatever they THINK does the least amount of harm. Most people would firstly go and try and steal something... doesn't matter that it's gonna cause 3 people to starve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T16:24:49-07:00","id":512384,"title":"","content":"People consent to harm all the time. Masochists, tattoos, piercings, body modification. If you take the lethal damage to mean 'harm' instead of being a mechanical representation of blood loss, there is still nothing immoral about harm done <b><i>with</i></b> consent. And addiction does not invalidate consent. That is, if an alcoholic orders wine at a restaurant, the waiter has consent to provide that wine even though the alcoholic is an addict. As the vampire is ideally controlling the space between 'doses' to protect his or her Blood Doll, I'd argue feeding is less immoral than giving an alcoholic booze.<br /> <br /> I doubt anyone will say that feeding is doing anyone a favor except the vampire, but done willingly it is a very pleasant experience for the mortal and the harm caused is not really any worse than anything listed at the beginning of this post. Due to this, I imagine you could get a herd without using any mind-control whatsoever. You just need to find the right type of individual.<br /> <br /> So I maintain that you can ethically feed as a vampire. It's just almost never going to happen. It's the providence of a Humanity 10 vampire to be that strict with one's feeding.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T19:29:13-07:00","id":512482,"title":"","content":"If I were turning into a cold corpse, with all the sensory deprivation (and accentuation) that comes with it, not to mention the psychological and biological changes taking place within my body (are Vampires always in a state of pain from the fact that their stomachs have shrivelled up?), the last thing I would do is philosophize about how my meal feels like.<br /> <br /> To understand how Vampires feel and <b>actually</b> react to their newfound states, take our world <b>realistically</b> (talk to some people suffering amidst urban decay, some from endangered communities, a couple of people living under capitalist crises and exploitation, perhaps join a facebook support group), then add upon it the layer that is called the World of <b>Darkness</b> (like our own, only darker and eviller). God, the Sabbat makes so much sense now that I think about it...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-12T20:34:03-07:00","id":512510,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512183#post512183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what makes a cow's life worth less than a human?</div> </div> </div> </div>If a mage makes a sentient cow, feeding from it would be just as bad as feeding from a human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512384#post512384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but done willingly it is a very pleasant experience for the mortal</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of a problem in itself, since it's known to cause addiction...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":815,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","user":"Kazorh","date":". 05-12-2015, 11:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/815-kazorh","name":"Kazorh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar815_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T00:12:48-07:00","id":512684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512482#post512482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">then add upon it the layer that is called the World of <b>Darkness</b> (like our own, only darker and eviller).</div> </div> </div> </div>This part is a relic from oWoD, and while this was used in the very first books of nWoD it has been droped since. The world is not &quot;darker and eviller&quot; by default.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T01:14:17-07:00","id":512718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512482#post512482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">are Vampires always in a state of pain from the fact that their stomachs have shrivelled up?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Why would their stomach even do that? It's the one bit they actually still use in some manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T06:04:03-07:00","id":512847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kazorh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512510#post512510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a mage makes a sentient cow, feeding from it would be just as bad as feeding from a human.</div> </div> </div> </div> I doubt that. Some scientists are calling dolphins sentient beings in the real world, and I would have zero qualms about killing and feeding from a dolphin if it was something I needed to survive. Why should I feel differently about a cow that will stop being sentient the moment the magic expires or is dispelled?<br /> <br /> We, as a people, are hardwired to care about our own species. Feeding from a human is problematic for a vampire because, lets face it, many still think part of them is still human (thus, Humanity). But non-human sentient species aren't something I think would be an issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's kind of a problem in itself, since it's known to cause addiction... </div> </div> </div> For some Daeva. We have an actual merit to represent an addictive Kiss now.<br /> <br /> Sure, there are some people that will become addicted to anyone's Kiss, but then, some people become addicted to regular sex, gambling, adrenaline, and any number of mundane sources of pleasure. I don't think we should say the Kiss is on par with an addictive substance, however, without the Kiss of the Succubus merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 05-13-2015, 09:08 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T07:10:37-07:00","id":512894,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512684#post512684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This part is a relic from oWoD, and while this was used in the very first books of nWoD it has been droped since. The world is not &quot;darker and eviller&quot; by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the monsters that inhabit the World of Darkness and the fact that it still is a horror game I very much doubt that it is not a darker version of RL <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> The very name of the game mentions it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T07:28:52-07:00","id":512899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512684#post512684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This part is a relic from oWoD, and while this was used in the very first books of nWoD it has been droped since. The world is not &quot;darker and eviller&quot; by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like Madfox11 said, just adding the supernatural to our world, ipso facto makes it a terrifying place. How do you think all these supernaturals react with those groups of every population that would, otherwise, in mortal life jump aboard the cult or extremist wagon?<br /> <br /> Again, nothing against overly-humanized superheroes with slightly dark powers stories, but isn't that quite the point that was extensively used against cWoD in the past? Dark superheroes. Why humanize (badly) something which cannot be humanized.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No. Why would their stomach even do that? It's the one bit they actually still use in some manner. </div> </div> </div>Maybe because they are walking corpses and almost every internal organ is dried up of every vital fluid other than blood? Vitae is not stored in the stomach, mind you. I think it is a very, very, very valid point to ask how a Vampire feels on those first nights of the embrace. I imagine the weirdness would be enough to scare the crap out of many a good neonates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T07:37:27-07:00","id":512908,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm not saying that World of Darkness isn't a worse place then our own. But it's not because EVERYTHING Is worse and more evil. It's because of the monsters lurking in the dark <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:12:04-07:00","id":512925,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512908#post512908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I'm not saying that World of Darkness isn't a worse place then our own. But it's not because EVERYTHING Is worse and more evil. It's because of the monsters lurking in the dark <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed., or at least the way I like to do it.<br /> <br /> IMHO, I think White Wolf has an (&quot;obligation&quot; isn't the right word, but I can't think of it) to support a broad range of play styles. They're not really obligated to do it, they're obligated to cleave to their artistic vision whether or not I like it. All that being said, White Wolf is THE only game in town for playing-as-monsters role-playing. There are a ton of active, supported, Fantasy (D&amp;D) - style RPG's, but other than Dresden Files, which has a very narrow focus and requires you to buy into Fate, theve done it right and their de-facto monopoly on the genre speaks to that. So, it always makes me happy when I can skew a Vampire game from Angel to 30 Days of Night or anything in between.<br /> <br /> That's what blew me away with the Mirrors books. In addition to generating some of the best mechanics ever (look at the Brutality dice thing for Humanity), it gives the GM a super toolkit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T08:37:32-07:00","id":512945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512899#post512899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it is a very, very, very valid point to ask how a Vampire feels on those first nights of the embrace.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not saying it's not a valid question. But the answer is very definitely no. You know how I know this? Because if a body part such as the stomach - which vamps don't actually need - caused them constant pain, then they would just <i>remove it.</i><br /> <br /> What probably happen is that they use that ability to control where their blood flows to pump up any bits that would hurt if dehydrated. I mean it's true that they don't <i>generally </i>store blood in their stomach, but if they wanted to they totally could. So keeping it inflated and moist wouldn't be an issue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T09:50:08-07:00","id":513009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>stylanski</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512899#post512899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, nothing against overly-humanized superheroes with slightly dark powers stories, but isn't that quite the point that was extensively used against cWoD in the past? Dark superheroes. Why humanize (badly) something which cannot be humanized.</div> </div> </div> </div>Weird, I had the opposite issue w/ a lot of cWoD. People wanted to play unrepentant monsters, so you got this massive proliferation of &quot;paths.&quot; You lost the original awesomeness of 1st Edition only (at least for me).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T10:47:44-07:00","id":513050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Archivist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512925#post512925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IMHO, I think White Wolf has an (&quot;obligation&quot; isn't the right word, but I can't think of it) to support a broad range of play styles. They're not really obligated to do it, they're obligated to cleave to their artistic vision whether or not I like it. All that being said, White Wolf is THE only game in town for playing-as-monsters role-playing. There are a ton of active, supported, Fantasy (D&amp;D) - style RPG's, but other than Dresden Files, which has a very narrow focus and requires you to buy into Fate, theve done it right and their de-facto monopoly on the genre speaks to that. So, it always makes me happy when I can skew a Vampire game from Angel to 30 Days of Night or anything in between.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. It really bums me out when I hear people say stuff like 'that faction is only for NPCs,' or 'those guys aren't meant to be playable.'<br /> <br /> I mean it makes sense for some things like rocks and idigam but why shouldn't one be able to play a VII vampire slayer or a Belial's Brood temptress? Obviously a ST or group has the final say and it can depend a lot on a type of game, but they shouldn't be collectively off the table for every group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-13-2015, 01:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T11:43:11-07:00","id":513165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513050#post513050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. It really bums me out when I hear people say stuff like 'that faction is only for NPCs,' or 'those guys aren't meant to be playable.'<br /> <br /> I mean it makes sense for some things like rocks and idigam but why shouldn't one be able to play a VII vampire slayer or a Belial's Brood temptress? Obviously a ST or group has the final say and it can depend a lot on a type of game, but they shouldn't be collectively off the table for every group.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a little like playing evil alignments in D&amp;D. There's nothing stopping you from playing Chaotic Evil if the group is cool with it. The books are just written with the assumption that most groups will play all good or neutral aligned parties. Likewise, WoD is written with the assumption that most groups will play as the protagonist factions. But if you want to play a member of VII, or an Ivory Claw, or a Seer, go for it, as long as your group doesn't mind. I actually think nWoD is better about this than a lot of RPGs because of its toolbox approach, and they even make books specifically about their antagonist groups with advice on using them as PCs. Heck, the Seers are going to be in the Paths section rather than the Antagonists section in Awakening 2e. And it's looking like Belial's Brood is going to be in Secrets of the Covenants as a heretical faction of the Lanea et Sanctum. Sure, Oath of the Worthless One marks you as kill on sight for other Sanctified if they find out you've performed it, but I figure if you want to play Brood, you're probably not bothered by Lancers wanting you dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-13-2015, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:16:29-07:00","id":513219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513165#post513165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And it's looking like Belial's Brood is going to be in Secrets of the Covenants as a heretical faction of the Lanea et Sanctum. Sure, Oath of the Worthless One marks you as kill on sight for other Sanctified if they find out you've performed it, but I figure if you want to play Brood, you're probably not bothered by Lancers wanting you dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the Brood still has multiple subfactions, I think it makes more sense for a subfaction to be a heretical splinter of the Lancea et Sanctum, than for the whole Brood, as the some parts of the Brood are thematically too far removed from the Sanctum.<br /> <br /> But we'll see when the book arrives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:21:13-07:00","id":513224,"title":"","content":"Yeah. I could see the Brood as having a sub faction in every covenant.<br /> <br /> And I'm not saying every book should be the equivalent to the Book of Vile Darkness, but I like having those options just as much as I do the opposite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-13-2015, 03:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T12:37:40-07:00","id":513235,"title":"","content":"Yea... I like that you can play it all sorts of ways. I think that's a good thing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T13:22:21-07:00","id":513259,"title":"","content":"The clanbooks touch slightly on what you feel like after the Embrace. I don't think it's constant pain, but it's very strange and unpleasant. Most people don't dwell on this much, but we experience all sorts of little sensations based on our bodies doing body business. Right now, for instance, I can feel my pulse a little bit because of the way my wrist is resting, there's the occasional bubbling sensation in my stomach, my eyes are a little dry, and I'm breathing normally. I feel all that, but I'm so used to it that I barely notice.<br /> <br /> If the Embrace stops all of those processes, then I'm going to feel weirdly numb and disconnected from my body... only to be pulled back into it by the need for blood that I can feel not just in my stomach, but in my bones and muscles and really everywhere. Being hungry feels like being hungry, but also like insomnia and cold and all sorts of other things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 05-13-2015, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:44:17-07:00","id":513332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=512847#post512847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I doubt that. Some scientists are calling dolphins sentient beings in the real world, and I would have zero qualms about killing and feeding from a dolphin if it was something I needed to survive. Why should I feel differently about a cow that will stop being sentient the moment the magic expires or is dispelled?</div> </div> </div> </div>Really? Cetaceans are quite intelligent. I'd have problem eating dolphins or whales.<br /> Dogs are said to about as smart as a 3 year old, Chimps about a 5 or 6 year old.<br /> Would you eat either of them? Oh yeah we can teach apes sign language.<br /> Elephants mourn their dead? How much smart do you have to be to do that?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.onegreenplanet.org/animalsandnature/human-intelligence-versus-whales-and-dolphins/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.onegreenplanet.org/wp-content/uploads/2014/12/orca.jpg?fit=1600%2C1066&amp;ssl=1\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.onegreenplanet.org/animalsandnature/human-intelligence-versus-whales-and-dolphins/\" target=\"_blank\"> Whales and Dolphins Might Be The Smartest Animals </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.onegreenplanet.org/animalsandnature/human-intelligence-versus-whales-and-dolphins/\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.onegreenplanet.org/animalsandnature/human-intelligence-versus-whales-and-dolphins/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> While humans, as a species, are pretty smart, studies show that cetaceans might have us beat! </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://us.whales.org/whales-and-dolphins/brain-power\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://us.whales.org/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2020/11/wdc-logo.png\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://us.whales.org/whales-and-dolphins/brain-power\" target=\"_blank\"> Page not found - Whale &amp; Dolphin Conservation USA </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://us.whales.org/whales-and-dolphins/brain-power\" target=\"_blank\"> http://us.whales.org/whales-and-dolphins/brain-power </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:45:49-07:00","id":513333,"title":"","content":"Well, in parts of the world, Chimps, Monkeys and Dogs are delicacies. Been to some of those places. Experienced some of the cuisine. Wouldn't do it here, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:48:20-07:00","id":513336,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, how unintelligent does a person have to be before they're okay to eat?<br /> <br /> And keep in mind a vampire with animalism can talk to a dog, a cat, a dolphin or a cow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:54:57-07:00","id":513340,"title":"","content":"The capacity to &quot;speak&quot; does not indicate intelligence. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T14:56:04-07:00","id":513341,"title":"","content":"No, but a vampire can become as close to a dog, a cat, a dolphin or a cow as a human might a dog or other human. Even a plant can become an extension of a vampire's life.<br /> <br /> They work on different levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:19:58-07:00","id":513354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=502512#post502512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally feel like its a feature that the Covenants are kind of unappealing to someone trying to be a &quot;good&quot; vampire. Many neonates are likely to have exactly the same reaction, and be pretty hesitant to get involved with any of them.<br /> <br /> But the fact is that vampires <i>are</i> monsters. Feeding hurts people; sometimes only a little, sometimes more than a little. So, at the very least, every vampire is a serial assaulter. Picking up a mortal in a bar under false pretenses and proceeding to injure and abandon them is arguably sexual assault. And, eventually, every vampire loses control, and somebody dies. There's a decent chance that, when this happens, the victim is someone the vampire cares about.<br /> <br /> <b>It could be argued that the most moral thing for a vampire to do is to end their own unnatural existence as soon as possible.</b> <i>Perhaps</i> they can manage to do more good than ill with their Requiem, at least for a while. But eventually the burden is likely to become too much to bear, and many may get to that point pretty quickly after their embrace. That's where the Covenants come in: they give the vampire a way to make sense of the harm they've done to people, and to &quot;live&quot; with it.<br /> <br /> Joining a Covenant is a way for a vampire to save themselves from total self-destruction, and all it costs is a little piece of their fraying soul...</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess it means I see no point of playing Vampire if the only 'moral' thing to do is commit suicide like as if it was never meant to be played at all so what's the point?<br /> <br /> I think it's better off to cast Vampire as unplayable NPC antagonists in the end.<br /> <br /> Or maybe this is the biggest problems I have with the personal horror theme even more so in Requiem than it is in Masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","user":"TunnelsofDarkness","date":". 05-13-2015, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","name":"TunnelsofDarkness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:23:35-07:00","id":513357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513354#post513354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it means I see no point of playing Vampire at all nor sounds like as if it was never meant to be played at all so what's the point?.<br /> <br /> I think it's better off to cast Vampire as unplayable NPC antagonists.<br /> <br /> Or maybe this is biggest problems with the personal horror theme even more so in Requiem than it is in Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's more like it means the game, as with everything, isn't for everybody. CatDoom has a particularly bleak view of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:39:29-07:00","id":513370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513357#post513357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's more like it means the game, as with everything, isn't for everybody. CatDoom has a particularly bleak view of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well thing is, even though Vampires is one of the mythical creatures I like but like you said I don't think Requiem (or maybe even Masquerade I don't know) may not be the game for me but then again, what other alternatives do I have? Especially since choices are (or maybe) very limited at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","user":"TunnelsofDarkness","date":". 05-13-2015, 06:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","name":"TunnelsofDarkness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:44:57-07:00","id":513371,"title":"","content":"Well if you really believe vampires are an immoral blight on the world and the only moral act they can perform is to self-annihilation, you might want to look at Hunter, where you can commit the moral act for them.<br /> <br /> You can also appreciate that, like humans, vampires do what they do to survive and decide to do good with their life or bad on an individual basis.<br /> <br /> Otherwise there's vampire, werewolf, mage, promethean, changeling, geist, demon, mummy, the 'lesser' games of skinchangers and immortals and possessed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:48:15-07:00","id":513372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513354#post513354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it means I see no point of playing Vampire if the only 'moral' thing to do is commit suicide like as if it was never meant to be played at all so what's the point?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The point is that that's <i>not </i>the only moral thing. If what little harm feeding does bothers you, that means there's a lot of shit in the world of darkness a hell of a lot worse than you. And unlike most people, you have the power to stop it. <br /> <br /> Fuck suicide. Go fight a strix or something. Worse case scenario you're dead anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:53:34-07:00","id":513375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513371#post513371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if you really believe vampires are an immoral blight on the world and the only moral act they can perform is to self-annihilation, you might want to look at Hunter, where you can commit the moral act for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't exactly believe that but however I just pointing out that Reqiuem's extreme version of the personal horror theme leads to that ultimate conclusion where one is better off playing as a Hunter and Vampires as antagonist where genocide is the only solution apparently.<br /> <br /> Unless of course if the Personal Horror theme is removed and make Vampires somewhat have redeemable aspects to them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","name":"TunnelsofDarkness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T15:54:46-07:00","id":513376,"title":"","content":"Tone can vary a lot, even within one chronicle.<br /> <br /> &quot;The only moral thing for a vampire to do is commit suicide&quot; is something that I hear repeated a lot, and I don't think it's true. A lot of us benefit in some way from bad things in the lives of others. Not usually from actual blood loss, but in very real ways. Often, the benefits aren't even essential the way eating is. I don't think that means that we should kill ourselves, or that anyone involved should feel that their lives are futile. I don't even think that suicide or futility are the most natural exaggerations to put into the game world.<br /> <br /> For my home games, I take both a pretty horrific and a pretty optimistic view of the Requiem. There are terrible things in the world. Those things will happen to you, and you may do those things, but you are not inherently one of them. The World of Darkness has room for both hope and tragedy, and which you find depends both on your choices and your perspective.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 05-13-2015, 06:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:09:36-07:00","id":513386,"title":"","content":"The personal horror theme doesn't preclude redeeming aspects. <br /> <br /> Vampires have to swim against the moral current for sure, but they can absolutely do it. Most PCs I've run games for, and played alongside were, on the balance, positive forces. Maintaining even a moderate humanity means you're not likely to be some kind of unrepentant blight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:10:47-07:00","id":513387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513375#post513375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't exactly believe that but however I just pointing out that Reqiuem's extreme version of the personal horror theme leads to that ultimate conclusion where one is better off playing as a Hunter and Vampires as antagonist where genocide is the only solution apparently.<br /> <br /> Unless of course if the Personal Horror theme is removed and make Vampires somewhat have redeemable aspects to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you think personal horror is?<br /> <br /> I ask because you seem to have a negative view of it. It can exist side by side with redemption, and doesn't have to lead to an 'ultimate conclusion' where genocide and annihilation of the self are the only options. It's not the conclusion people made of Angel, or Edward or Spider-man.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:17:00-07:00","id":513390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513336#post513336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alternatively, how unintelligent does a person have to be before they're okay to eat?<br /> <br /> And keep in mind a vampire with animalism can talk to a dog, a cat, a dolphin or a cow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Conversations like this are why I shouldn't be a contestant on Survivor. I'd probably be trying to eat the other contestants in under a week.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/460-rani-neferet","name":"Rani Neferet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar460_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"971"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:18:19-07:00","id":513404,"title":"","content":"To shorten various points I've made: <i>Vampire: The Requiem</i> presents a lot of obstacles, but overcoming them or not is what a game is about, not a conclusion we've packaged for you.<br /> <br /> But, since we're talking about vampire suicide, here's <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KIYiGA_rIls\" target=\"_blank\">my favorite song about it</a>. It's even got Carthians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:29:06-07:00","id":513448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Smarmy Vamp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513386#post513386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The personal horror theme doesn't preclude redeeming aspects.</div> </div> </div> </div>There can be no true despair without hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:31:47-07:00","id":513450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513354#post513354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I guess it means I see no point of playing Vampire if the only 'moral' thing to do is commit suicide like as if it was never meant to be played at all so what's the point?<br /> <br /> I think it's better off to cast Vampire as unplayable NPC antagonists in the end.<br /> <br /> Or maybe this is the biggest problems I have with the personal horror theme even more so in Requiem than it is in Masquerade.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game de facto revolves around the though decisions around choosing between Man and Beast, horror and hope for a quite elusive better tomorrow. Like a person on a diet that slips, but keeps hoping tomorrow will be the day he sticks with it. If you want to play heroes with powers, that's perfectly acceptable (and you'll find people to do so). I suppose the point of some of us here is that the writing is not <b>supposed</b> to automatically cater to that particular theme, since you can already do that pretty easily yourself.<br /> <br /> That said, and I can't believe I'm actually using a TF2 reference here, but just because your mortal moral viewpoint sees Vampires as irredeemable monsters doesn't mean your characters will see themselves as such.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WUhOnX8qt3I\" data-code=\"WUhOnX8qt3I\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/WUhOnX8qt3I/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:33:23-07:00","id":513451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513448#post513448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There can be no true despair without hope.</div> </div> </div> </div>The vampire life is not bereft of hope.<br /> <br /> Also I guess I'm just <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=W1WnrjciO8c\" target=\"_blank\">old</a>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:40:14-07:00","id":513461,"title":"","content":"I think the only moral thing a vampire can do is walk out into the sun and burn. There are Buddhists that believe it is not moral to kill animals, including bugs. There are people that when forced to eat other people or starve chose long pig. Morality is personal and therefore subjective when applied to a group of people. It could be that a vampire sees their parasitic existence as necessary to further a greater good. A vampire has all of eternity to do good, or evil. Vampires have power by virtue of their existence. They have time beyond comprehension. It could be that choosing to end that existence and foregoing all the good a vampire could do is not moral. Using people as food is not human, but using other animals is human. Vampires are not human, although they sometimes try to be. How successful they are and how that success is even defined is the game. There is a great deal of room when answering those questions. You can play superhero vampires in Requiem. You can play monsters playing at humanity too. Those are not mutually exclusive either. It's complex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1526-diggs","name":"Diggs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T16:53:06-07:00","id":513469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513375#post513375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't exactly believe that but however I just pointing out that Reqiuem's extreme version of the personal horror theme leads to that ultimate conclusion where one is better off playing as a Hunter and Vampires as antagonist where genocide is the only solution apparently.<br /> <br /> Unless of course if the Personal Horror theme is removed and make Vampires somewhat have redeemable aspects to them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't agree with Cat Doom's extreme view on the personal horror of Requiem. I mean, if that's what Cat Doom enjoys in their game, more power to them, but I really don't think that's the intended message of the setting. It's certainly not how I run my games, and it doesn't have to be the way you run yours.<br /> <br /> The personal horror of vampire, at least for me, is in losing touch with the human experience. A newly embraced vampire probably isn't going to immediately get all woe-is-me about being immortal and having super powers. Hell, I'd be pretty stoked about the whole deal. But they slowly begin to realize that the reality of being a vampire is worse than they may have initially thought. Maybe they were a bit squicked out by the idea of feeding at first, so they tried doing the blood bag thing, or sneaking out to a farm and draining a cow a few times. But eventually out of necessity, or curiosity, or peer pressure, they tried feeding on a human. Surprise! Not only is it not as bad as they thought, it <i>feels incredible</i>. But that's the problem - having been human only recently, they still have human ideas about morality and ethics. On an intellectual level, they know it's wrong. They know they should be horrified at what they're doing. But <i>god damn if it isn't the best thing they've ever felt.</i>.<br /> <br /> Being confronted with this cognitive dissonance of knowing they should feel revolted at what they're doing, but instead feeling elated, they could deal with this identity crisis in a few ways. They <i>could</i> come to Cat Doom's conclusion that they are doomed to bring nothing but harm to the world and the only solution is to meet the sun. I would call that the high humanity route. Or, they could harden themselves, justifying what they're doing as no worse than a human eating a steak, adjusting their worldview to account for the fact that they're not human any more, and the same rules don't apply to them. I would call that the low humanity route.<br /> <br /> The realities of vampiric existance lead to one of these crisies of humanity after another, and the covenants exist, in part, to help those young vampires struggling to come to terms with what they are cope. They offer context for the confused neonate, give them structure and purpose, a way to put their newfound monstrousness to productive ends.<br /> <br /> Now, this generally means Humanity loss - their worldviews may make a certain kind of sense, but they are certainly not human worldviews. But inhuman doesn't have to mean evil. For every Acolyte making human sacrifices to heathen blood gods, there is another who merely wants to do as she will and harm none. For every Sanctified who uses religion as a tool for fear and control, there is another who just wants to help other Damned souls realize that God still has a plan for them. For every Defiant who performs cruel and unusual experiments on human subjects in hopes of learning new ways to become a more powerful monster, there is another looking within for personal enlightenment, seeking to become something more than just an undead parasite. For every firebrand who just wants to burn this motherfucker down, there is another who truly cares about making vampire society better, make it so that a politically-minded vampire doesn't have to lie, cheat, and backstab their way to the top. For every Invictus who uses the masquerade to infiltrate human power structures for their own personal gain, there is another who defends the masquerade to protect humans, because they know for most people it's safer not to know.<br /> <br /> EDIT: to clarify, I don't mean it's a literal 1:1 ratio, I just liked the way &quot;for every ____, there is a _____&quot; sounded.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 05-13-2015, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:06:46-07:00","id":513475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513469#post513469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or, they could harden themselves, justifying what they're doing as no worse than a human eating a steak, adjusting their worldview to account for the fact that they're not human any more, and the same rules don't apply to them. I would call that the low humanity route.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd call that the &quot;mid-humanity route,&quot; and add a third option: they can realize their new power makes them gods among men, none of the old rules apply to them, and they can kill, maim, and torture anyone they want with zero consequences. That's the low-humanity route.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:25:33-07:00","id":513486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513475#post513475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd call that the &quot;mid-humanity route,&quot; and add a third option: they can realize their new power makes them gods among men, none of the old rules apply to them, and they can kill, maim, and torture anyone they want with zero consequences. That's the low-humanity route.</div> </div> </div> </div>However if they continue down that route, they'll eventually hit humanity 0 and become a Dragur which is actually the main consequence which they'll become the monsters they're truly are as if they were like that all along due to the beast. So it means either path you take, you're basically screwed which is why it's rather pointless to play in the first place.<br /> <br /> Or rather this is the main reason I don't like the Personal Horror theme where the whole humanity system and the beast is designed to punish you especially if you take the &quot;gods amoung man&quot; and &quot;mass murderer&quot; route (well my major beef is that other supernaturals and mortals can kill anyone they want without the fear of becoming a complete monster while Vampires are confined to some Abrahamic worldview of morality) as if and not only that, I don't like the idea of &quot;loosing control&quot; as well which I think I said before that it pays parallels to excuses like &quot;The Devil Made me Do it&quot; or &quot;It's my Nature I can't help it&quot; and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5708,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","user":"TunnelsofDarkness","date":". 05-13-2015, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5708-tunnelsofdarkness","name":"TunnelsofDarkness","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:44:00-07:00","id":513506,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513486#post513486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However if they continue down that route, they'll eventually hit humanity 0 and become a Dragur which is actually the main consequence which they'll become the monsters they're truly are as if they were like that all along due to the beast. So it means either path you take, you're basically screwed which is why it's rather pointless to play in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most paths don't lead that way, ErikModi specifically called out a monstrous path, and even that isn't necessarily going to lead to humanity 0. And humanity can be regained.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or rather this is the main reason I don't like the Personal Horror theme where the whole humanity system and the beast is designed to punish you especially if you take the &quot;gods amoung man&quot; and &quot;mass murderer&quot; route (well my major beef is that other supernaturals and mortals can kill anyone they want without the fear of becoming a complete monster while Vampires are confined to some Abrahamic worldview of morality) as if and not only that, I don't like the idea of &quot;loosing control&quot; as well which I think I said before that it pays parallels to excuses like &quot;The Devil Made me Do it&quot; or &quot;It's my Nature I can't help it&quot; and such. </div> </div> </div>Also, that's not personal horror, that's just a certain type of game, and not the only one that can be played. As Rose Bailey said, that's a tone you can take with it, but it doesn't have to be the only one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:44:54-07:00","id":513507,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that the Beast will attempt to prevent you from killing yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T17:56:18-07:00","id":513535,"title":"","content":"If you're doing it with fire or sunlight, that's right, in the sense that you'll probably frenzy and try to run away.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:48:40-07:00","id":513579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513486#post513486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However if they continue down that route, they'll eventually hit humanity 0 and become a Dragur which is actually the main consequence which they'll become the monsters they're truly are as if they were like that all along due to the beast. So it means either path you take, you're basically screwed which is why it's rather pointless to play in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all. Humanity is not a one-way street, it can be regained. Sure, if you turn your back on any hope of being anything but a monster, you're screwed. The same can be said of actual humans. Being a good person is hard work, especially when you're a literal monster who eats people. But it seems rather nihlistic to say that because it's possible to become a Draugr if you don't work hard enough to maintain your Humanity, there's no point in even playing. The struggle to avoid that end (which is far from inevitable) is what matters most.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513486#post513486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or rather this is the main reason I don't like the Personal Horror theme where the whole humanity system and the beast is designed to punish you especially if you take the &quot;gods amoung man&quot; and &quot;mass murderer&quot; route (well my major beef is that other supernaturals and mortals can kill anyone they want without the fear of becoming a complete monster while Vampires are confined to some Abrahamic worldview of morality)</div> </div> </div> </div>So first of all, Humanity loss is not a punishment, it's a dramatic device. World of Darkness is very big on the idea that what's bad for the character is not always bad for the player, and in fact it's often good for the player because it creates conflict and makes for good stories. Especially in 2nd edition, which actually mechanically incentivizes players to allow bad things to happen to their characters. Second, you should take a closer look at Humanity, because it is absolutely not an Abrahamic system of morality, at least not in 2nd edition. It's not even a system of morality <i>at all</i>. Humanity Breaking Points happen when a character is forced to face the fact that they're not human any more. Vampires spend a lot of time pretending to be human - not just to disguise themselves from others, but to convince themselves that they're not monsters. Humanity Breaking Points happen for things like surviving something that would kill a human, spending too long without human interaction, depriving someone of consent with your supernatural powers, seeing people you knew in life die of old age, or on a larger scale, watching civilizations fall. Yes, they also happen for things like murder, because murder is really not part of the usual human experience (and in my personal head-cannon, because they don't feel guilty about it, and that freaks them out because they know that they logically should), not because it's immoral. Finally, no, humans and other supernaturals cannot just kill anyone they want without fear of becoming a complete monster. In 1e at least, almost every template had Murder as a sin against what ever stat was their equivalent to Morality, and they became unplayable when their Morality-stat reached 0. Sometimes they became monsters, sometimes they were driven mad, but in general, Morality-stat 0 meant game over. 2nd edition has challenged that status quo a bit, but having a low Integrity-stat (or either extreme high or low for werewolves) still causes complications. Not to mention the fact that someone who commits wanton murder with no compunctions is pretty much a monster regardless of whether or not the rules call them one.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TunnelsofDarkness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513486#post513486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as if and not only that, I don't like the idea of &quot;loosing control&quot; as well which I think I said before that it pays parallels to excuses like &quot;The Devil Made me Do it&quot; or &quot;It's my Nature I can't help it&quot; and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>A vampire is still responsible for their actions in Frenzy just as a human with a bad temper is still responsible for their actions when they fly off the handle. &quot;The Beast Made me Do it&quot; is just as poor of an excuse for them as &quot;The Devil Made me Do it&quot; is for us. It's just there so that, no matter how human a vampire tries to be, they'll still have to struggle with the fact that they could flip out and kill some one if they get too hungry or too grumpy. It insures that they have to take precautions to protect the people around them from themselves, just like real people with anger issues have to do. On the subject of superheroes, I can think of at least one who's all about avoiding the fight because he knows he'll win.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T18:52:53-07:00","id":513582,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">It has come to my attention that TunnelsofDarkness was a sockpuppet account for another user who was previously permanently banned. They have been re-banned for violating rule 7 (maintain only one account), not for any comments made in this thread.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T19:02:22-07:00","id":513587,"title":"","content":"I thought his arguments sounded familiar.<br /> <br /> Here's a picture of a vampire. Don't worry, he's not dead.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"http://4.bp.blogspot.com/-yty4ZwP_l48/UD81irdKUCI/AAAAAAAAAok/6D4IdCBOHZ4/s1600/NATC_LOOKER_1.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T19:28:05-07:00","id":513607,"title":"","content":"Well, that's unfortunate. I think some really interesting ideas were starting to crop up, but the constant nay-saying was getting annoying.<br /> <br /> To respond, even though Tunnels won't see it. . . yeah, sure, behaving like a blood-soaked B-movie villain will eventually lead you to Humanity 0. That's why I specifically called it out as the <i>low-Humanity</i> path. &quot;Low,&quot; to my mind, being, say, 0-3.<br /> <br /> As for loss of Humanity being a punishment, it's no more a punishment than taking wounds in a combat situation. If a player has their character make choices that leads them into a violent conflict, then they should be prepared to accept the consequences of that scene, which could include lasting injuries and even character death. In <i>the exact same way</i>, a player who chooses to have their character act in a manner that consistently provokes Detachment rules should be prepared to accept the consequences of those decisions, which could include losing Humanity dots and their character becoming an unplayable Draugr. If you don't want your character become a Draugr, don't provoke Detachment rolls below a certain level. Simple.<br /> <br /> The one valid point is with Frenzy, which can take control away from the character long enough to provoke that last Breaking Point. However, let's be honest here. . . if you're at one Humanity, and the ST <i>forces</i> you into Frenzy and <i>makes</i> you do something to lose that last dot, and thus your character, your ST is a dick. Frenzy is a fairly rare thing, in my experience, and there are plenty of ways to stave it off or minimize the damage, so you can keep things from truly spinning out of control. In my opinion, Frenzy is best used as a kind of Sword of Damocles. . . always there, always something the characters (not necessarily the players) should be aware of on some level, but it should only rarely descend and make a particular vampire's unlife miserable.<br /> <br /> Also, nofather, LOVE the Jessica Rabbit vampire <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T19:29:52-07:00","id":513608,"title":"","content":"What's that from, nofather?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T19:35:58-07:00","id":513640,"title":"","content":"That's <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Looker_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Looker</a>, a member of the Outsiders. Though that particular picture was from the cover of National Comics: Looker, which detailed her reboot and made her a full fledged vampire instead of beating around the bush.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T19:54:08-07:00","id":513654,"title":"","content":"You know, this discussion reminded me of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=P1QUZzeZoPQ\" target=\"_blank\">this song</a> a player of mine requested, after the soon-to-be fledgling coterie survived quite a nasty plot some elder threw at them. (It's from Borderlands 2, which I eventually ended up playing)<br /> <br /> At the end of that scene, they had witnessed just how deep the elder's cobweb ran. Amidst a Gotham-esque (the TV series) situation, where good guys were bad, white was black, good was evil, they just looked around and saw each other bloody and tired of fighting a battle in the war that had only just began. That's how a group of players who barely knew each other ended up being friends too. Easily one of my favourite gaming moments. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-13T20:36:01-07:00","id":513691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513640#post513640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Looker_(comics)\" target=\"_blank\">Looker</a>, a member of the Outsiders. Though that particular picture was from the cover of National Comics: Looker, which detailed her reboot and made her a full fledged vampire instead of beating around the bush.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay. I knew the character, but didn't recognize her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T02:25:03-07:00","id":513978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ErikModi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513607#post513607\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one valid point is with Frenzy, which can take control away from the character long enough to provoke that last Breaking Point. However, let's be honest here. . . if you're at one Humanity, and the ST <i>forces</i> you into Frenzy and <i>makes</i> you do something to lose that last dot, and thus your character, your ST is a dick.</div> </div> </div> </div>That one does require a dramatic failure. Especially at that level. You need to do some pretty horrible shit to lose your last dot.<br /> <br /> So we are talking a literal &quot;Shit I rolled a 1&quot; moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T03:35:44-07:00","id":514006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=513978#post513978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That one does require a dramatic failure. Especially at that level. You need to do some pretty horrible shit to lose your last dot.<br /> <br /> So we are talking a literal &quot;Shit I rolled a 1&quot; moment.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yup, if you're losing your last one, you're what... killing your touchstone looks like most probable? Anyways, to get into frenzy you must be stuffed with a frenzy trigger. For the sake of the argument we could say that anything which gives a penalty to the frenzy roll might count as a trigger. So, you're in the presence of your touchstone and you you're so careless that you get wounded/you're starving and you're low on WP to make the frenzy probable? Now, to kill your touchstone, he's likely the provocation, which gives you bonus dice. Getting into this situation isn't just T being a dick. It's you going into such a risky situation or failing other stuff numerious times beforehand. Why? just why? Not to mention that getting to Humanity 1 is an achievement in and of itself. <br /> Alternative breaking points are also very inprobably. Mass man slaughter? When does that happen in a single frenzy? <br /> If you manage to go down to Humanity 1, I'd say that your choices are leading you there, not a dick gm. Losing those lower humanity points is super hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T09:52:44-07:00","id":514238,"title":"","content":"I'd say the most likely way to lose your last dot of Humanity in Frenzy would be Diablerie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T09:58:52-07:00","id":514255,"title":"","content":"That only happens if you set it as the goal yourself when riding the wave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T10:37:12-07:00","id":514302,"title":"","content":"Well, that was basically my point, in response to the idea (which may not have been Tunnel's point) that spiraling Humanity combined with &quot;loss of PC control&quot; in Frenzy could lead to a character being unplayable. It's <i>incredibly</i> unlikely to occur in normal play, and if it happens basically because the ST says so, then that is a bad ST.<br /> <br /> You might lose a dot here or there due to Frenzying in the wrong place at the wrong time, but you aren't going to go from &quot;average newbie vamp&quot; to &quot;mindless drinking machine&quot; JUST because of Frenzies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T10:49:10-07:00","id":514334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=514255#post514255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That only happens if you set it as the goal yourself when riding the wave.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, nevermind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T11:19:18-07:00","id":514345,"title":"","content":"Or if you're Diablerie addicted, I bet it'll happen more often then on involuntary frenzies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T11:42:00-07:00","id":514356,"title":"","content":"Yeah, but those cases ain't ST being a dick. It's how things evolve. The whole &quot;if you lose your last dot due to frenzy your ST is a dick&quot; thing rubbed me in a really bad way...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T12:56:09-07:00","id":514413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=514356#post514356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, but those cases ain't ST being a dick. It's how things evolve. The whole &quot;if you lose your last dot due to frenzy your ST is a dick&quot; thing rubbed me in a really bad way...</div> </div> </div> </div>Roger that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T13:49:10-07:00","id":514442,"title":"","content":"That's also why I specifically called the ST FORCING you into Frenzy and MAKING you lose your last Humanity dot. It's a different case from things evolving that way out of the choices you had your character make, by which point whether the Detachment happened in Frenzy or not is still squarely on the player, voiding the &quot;loss of control&quot; argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T14:15:38-07:00","id":514484,"title":"","content":"But that's not any different than ST declaring that you were just killed by a lightning bolt from the sky. It's not something which actually warrants a discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T15:04:01-07:00","id":514538,"title":"","content":"More or less what I was driving at <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Frenzy &quot;loss of control&quot; meaning that your character's fate is pointless is incorrect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T18:49:02-07:00","id":514701,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure that I'd want activities during Frenzy to always result in a humanity check, particularly when it's this important. If I'm going to use the Humanity mechanic it's going to be to drive interesting choices.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5685-archivist","name":"Archivist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5685_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T19:05:13-07:00","id":514706,"title":"","content":"They don't. Frenzy is at least partially directed, it's not a mad 'kill everyone around you for no reason.'<br /> <br /> Though if you get a dramatic failure while trying to resist you keep frenzying until you reach a breaking point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T22:32:10-07:00","id":514832,"title":"","content":"I mean, according to the &quot;Who's Driving?&quot; sidebar, the player retains at least some control of the character, even if the character isn't in control of herself. The way I run it, the player retains essentially full control, they just can't take actions that don't directly contribute to achieving the goal of the Frenzy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-14T23:03:07-07:00","id":514840,"title":"","content":"Here's how I look at it.<br /> <br /> In World of Darkness games, the player's job at the table is to play her character and guide his story. If the character gets dumped by his boyfriend, she decides his reaction. If the character gets hit in the face with a tire iron, she decides if he strikes back. If the character has a plan to kill the Prince, she decides how he executes it.<br /> <br /> Frenzy is just one more kind of drama, one more situation to react to. Yes, the character is overwhelmed by his survival instincts, and his rationality is... limited. The player doesn't have a full range of options. But the character is still hers, and it's still her job -- and right -- to play him. Frenzy's placement in the same section as sunlight and fire is deliberate -- it's one of the curses vampires have to deal with. And players decide how their characters deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T07:50:15-07:00","id":515151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/501915-non-super-evil-vtr2?p=514840#post514840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's how I look at it.<br /> <br /> In World of Darkness games, the player's job at the table is to play her character and guide his story. If the character gets dumped by his boyfriend, she decides his reaction. If the character gets hit in the face with a tire iron, she decides if he strikes back. If the character has a plan to kill the Prince, she decides how he executes it.<br /> <br /> Frenzy is just one more kind of drama, one more situation to react to. Yes, the character is overwhelmed by his survival instincts, and his rationality is... limited. The player doesn't have a full range of options. But the character is still hers, and it's still her job -- and right -- to play him. Frenzy's placement in the same section as sunlight and fire is deliberate -- it's one of the curses vampires have to deal with. And players decide how their characters deal with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Literally the only time I've ever taken control away from a player was when they went into fear frenzy/rotsheck, and I flat out told them that no, their reaction to a burning rag coming right at them as to retreat to a safe distance and wait until it goes out (they were facing a vampire who used rags and a lighter to help their escape, get into a corridor or tunnel, set the rag alight, and even if frenzying you're likely to throw it behind you and run as fast as you can). They were fully allowed to do other things, as long as they didn't involved going near the fire.<br /> <br /> I see no reason to take away control for anger/hungry frenzy, but fear frenzy requires a level of 'no, you can't do that' with some groups.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T09:27:53-07:00","id":515246,"title":"","content":"That's part of the limited range of options though. You can say &quot;no, you can't do that&quot; without taking control of the character and saying &quot;this is what your character does.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T09:30:06-07:00","id":515248,"title":"","content":"What Charlaquin said. There's even a provision for breaking the boundaries and going outside the restrictions of a given frenzy (WP expenditure). It's just taxing, and you can't keep it up forever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/689-smarmy-vamp","name":"Smarmy Vamp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar689_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T09:49:36-07:00","id":515258,"title":"","content":"Exactly.<br /> <br /> The most memorable Frenzy I ever ran (back in VtM) was role-playing a vampire hunting after a particularly taxing battle. He went to a bar, found a nice pretty girl, convinced her to take a walk with him, and put the bite on her on a bridge. Since he had only three blood, he had to roll for Frenzy. . . failed. After much deliberation, I wound up flat-out telling the player that with a WP, he could perform ONE, and ONLY one, action. He could either lick the wound closed, in which case when the Frenzy &quot;came back&quot; he'd bite her again, or he could throw himself off the bridge, potentially sparing her life (he wanted to do both, and of course if he just let the Frenzy run it's course, he'd drink her dry.) This minor incident actually turned into a big deal, as he went by the hospital later to check on her, only to find a Tzimisce there Embracing her. He wound up having to take this young &quot;Clanless&quot; vampire under his wing, and the whole damn thing was his fault. I didn't call for a Humanity check (even though I probably should have), but it still created an interesting new wrinkle in this vampire's life.<br /> <br /> Now, the Frenzy rules in Requiem seem a lot more forgiving and open to interpretation than in Masquerade, so it might be plausible that, in the same situation, this vampire in Requiem could have licked the wound closed and fled the scene without endangering an innocent life. On the other hand, maybe he couldn't. Rule of Drama: want the complication, play it strict. Want the sense of narrowly averted disaster, play it loose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/4411-my-geist-gmc-updates\" target=\"_blank\">My Geist GMC Updates</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4348-my-infinite-macabre-goodies\" target=\"_blank\">My Infinite Macabre Goodies</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/4372-parasite-eve-the-third-birthday-chronicle\" target=\"_blank\">Parasite Eve: The Third Birthday Chronicle</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/899558-shamelessly-pimping-my-book\" target=\"_blank\">Shamelessly pimping my book</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/831-erikmodi","name":"ErikModi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-15T11:00:58-07:00","id":515300,"title":"","content":"One of my players let their character get Vinculum'd by a sort of madman of a vampire who proceeded to rewrite her memory of her pre-vampire life. Mostly by interjecting himself into it.<br /> <br /> But I had explained the basics of the idea to the player beforehand and asked if it was alright.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-15-2015, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}